# Security Requirements

Sentinel Scanner must only assess systems that the
user owns or has explicit authorization to test.

## Target Authorization

- Require explicit authorization confirmation.
- Restrict scans to registered targets.
- Enforce approved host and port scope.
- Validate every scan job independently.

## SSRF Protection

- Reject loopback addresses.
- Reject private network ranges by default.
- Reject link-local addresses.
- Block cloud metadata endpoints.
- Validate resolved IP addresses.
- Revalidate every redirect.
- Defend against DNS rebinding.
- Prevent access to internal infrastructure.

## Scanner Isolation

- Run scanning engines in isolated containers.
- Use restricted Linux capabilities.
- Avoid privileged containers.
- Apply CPU and memory limits.
- Restrict network egress.
- Never mount the Docker socket into scanner containers.

## Authentication

- Hash passwords securely using Argon2id.
- Use short-lived access tokens.
- Rotate refresh tokens.
- Revoke compromised tokens.
- Enforce authorization on every protected resource.

## General

- Never hardcode credentials.
- Never expose secrets in logs.
- Validate all external inputs.
- Apply rate limits.
- Audit security-sensitive operations.
- Prefer secure defaults.
